{%- comment -%}
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Rosalia · Funnel — "Human Wiring" mechanism article
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  A long-form mechanism piece for the flusher. Runs bare: the funnel
  suffix list in layout/theme.liquid strips the store header and footer,
  so this section owns the whole page.

  FOUR THINGS WERE CHANGED FROM THE SUPPLIED DRAFT, AND WHY

  1. The disclosure line at the top. The draft presented this as an
     independent publication ("Independent. No sponsorships. No paid
     placements.") that then recommends the publisher's own product.
     A business running a site that looks independent and endorses its
     own goods is exactly what the FTC's 2024 rule on consumer reviews
     bars (16 CFR §465.5, company-controlled review websites), and the
     undisclosed material connection is §255 on top. An advertorial is
     perfectly legal — an advertorial wearing a press badge is not. One
     line at the top fixes it and costs nothing else.

  2. Two citations were removed. "Demirbas et al., J Cosmet Dermatol,
     2025" and "Two Faces of Flushing, J Invest Dermatol, 2020" do not
     exist — searched for both, neither is real. The science that IS
     real carries the piece on its own: Yamasaki 2007 in Nature Medicine
     (KLK5 / cathelicidin, cited thousands of times) and Muto 2014 in
     JID (mast-cell ablation) are both genuine and are the two load-
     bearing claims anyway.

  3. The figures are captioned as illustrations, because that is what
     they are. Captioning a generated image "adapted from [study]" turns
     a drawing into fabricated evidence. They now say what they are: a
     drawing of a published mechanism.

  4. The reader letters were removed. Quotes attributed to "R., 47" and
     "J., 52" are testimonials from people who do not exist. Same rule
     that has applied to every other page on this store.

  Everything else — the argument, the structure, the typography, the
  voice — is the draft as supplied.
{%- endcomment -%}

